task: script-live-durable
agent: fable-persist
started: 2026-09-07
branch: feature/script-live-durable
worktree: ../okay-wt-durable

why: script-live-resume gave the reconnect (in memory, this process
  only) and filed the restart. The container already has the durable
  thing: `Sessions.persisted(store)` keeps a session's attributes
  across a restart, swept by TTL, clustered by `Sessions.shared`.

what: `Live.durable(init)(view)(update, push)(using Schema[S])` — an
  app whose state is a SESSION ATTRIBUTE (`okay.live.<id>`, CBOR in
  base64): `session(key, attrs, name)` reads it before the in-memory
  copy and writes it on Closed, through the Handle `Site.ws` binds
  from the socket's cookie — only a bound one, so a socket with a
  stale cookie mints nothing. A restart, a second node sharing the
  topic, the TTL sweep: all the session's, and now the app's. An app
  without a Schema keeps the in-memory reconnect. Test: two Sites over
  one store, the second resumes what the first reached.
